{"id":"copper-sun","title":"Copper Sun","author":"Countee Cullen","year":"1927","note":"Harlem poems of love, race, and the long tower.","minutes":182,"cover":"","coverAlt":"","scenes":[{"id":"s0","title":"From the Dark Tower","place":"From the Dark Tower","reentry":"(To Charles S. Johnson)","prompt":"What light does the poem hold?"},{"id":"s1","title":"Threnody for a Brown Girl","place":"Threnody for a Brown Girl","reentry":"EEP not, you who love her;","prompt":"What light does the poem hold?"}],"breaths":[{"id":"s0-0","sceneId":"s0","text":"(To Charles S. Johnson)"},{"id":"s0-1","sceneId":"s0","text":"We shall not always plant while others"},{"id":"s0-2","sceneId":"s0","text":"reap"},{"id":"s0-3","sceneId":"s0","text":"The golden increment of bursting fruit,"},{"id":"s0-4","sceneId":"s0","text":"Not always countenance, abject and mute,"},{"id":"s0-5","sceneId":"s0","text":"That lesser men should hold their brothers"},{"id":"s0-6","sceneId":"s0","text":"cheap;"},{"id":"s0-7","sceneId":"s0","text":"Not everlastingly while others sleep"},{"id":"s0-8","sceneId":"s0","text":"Shall we beguile their limbs with mellow"},{"id":"s0-9","sceneId":"s0","text":"flute,"},{"id":"s0-10","sceneId":"s0","text":"Not always bend to some more subtle brute;"},{"id":"s0-11","sceneId":"s0","text":"We were not made eternally to weep."},{"id":"s0-12","sceneId":"s0","text":"The night whose      sable breast relieves the"},{"id":"s0-13","sceneId":"s0","text":"stark,"},{"id":"s0-14","sceneId":"s0","text":"White stars is no less lovely being dark,"},{"id":"s0-15","sceneId":"s0","text":"And there are buds that cannot bloom at all"},{"id":"s0-16","sceneId":"s0","text":"In light, but crumple, piteous, and fall;"},{"id":"s0-17","sceneId":"s0","text":"So in the dark we hide the heart that bleeds,"},{"id":"s0-18","sceneId":"s0","text":"And wait, and tend our agonizing seeds."},{"id":"s1-0","sceneId":"s1","text":"EEP not, you who love her;"},{"id":"s1-1","sceneId":"s1","text":"What rebellious flow"},{"id":"s1-2","sceneId":"s1","text":"Grief undams shall recover"},{"id":"s1-3","sceneId":"s1","text":"Whom the gods bid gor"},{"id":"s1-4","sceneId":"s1","text":"Sorrow rising like a wall,"},{"id":"s1-5","sceneId":"s1","text":"Bitter, blasphemous,"},{"id":"s1-6","sceneId":"s1","text":"What avails it to recall"},{"id":"s1-7","sceneId":"s1","text":"Beauty back to usP"},{"id":"s1-8","sceneId":"s1","text":"Think not this grave shall keep her,"},{"id":"s1-9","sceneId":"s1","text":"This marriage-bed confine;"},{"id":"s1-10","sceneId":"s1","text":"Death may dig it deep and deeper;"},{"id":"s1-11","sceneId":"s1","text":"She shall climb it like a vine."},{"id":"s1-12","sceneId":"s1","text":"Body that was quick and sentient,"},{"id":"s1-13","sceneId":"s1","text":"Dear as thought or speech,"},{"id":"s1-14","sceneId":"s1","text":"Death could not with one trenchant"},{"id":"s1-15","sceneId":"s1","text":"Blow snatch out of reach."},{"id":"s1-16","sceneId":"s1","text":"She is nearer than the word"},{"id":"s1-17","sceneId":"s1","text":"Wasted on her now,"},{"id":"s1-18","sceneId":"s1","text":"Nearer than the swaying bird"},{"id":"s1-19","sceneId":"s1","text":"On its rhythmic bough."},{"id":"s1-20","sceneId":"s1","text":"Only were our faith as much"},{"id":"s1-21","sceneId":"s1","text":"As a mustard seed,"},{"id":"s1-22","sceneId":"s1","text":"4"},{"id":"s1-23","sceneId":"s1","text":"Aching, hungry hands might touch"},{"id":"s1-24","sceneId":"s1","text":"Her as they touch a reed."},{"id":"s1-25","sceneId":"s1","text":"Life who was not loth to trade her"},{"id":"s1-26","sceneId":"s1","text":"Unto death, has done"},{"id":"s1-27","sceneId":"s1","text":"Better than he planned, has made her"},{"id":"s1-28","sceneId":"s1","text":"Wise as Solomon."},{"id":"s1-29","sceneId":"s1","text":"Now she knows the Why and Wherefore,"},{"id":"s1-30","sceneId":"s1","text":"Troublous Whence and Whither,"},{"id":"s1-31","sceneId":"s1","text":"Why men strive and sweat, and care for"},{"id":"s1-32","sceneId":"s1","text":"Bays that droop and wither."},{"id":"s1-33","sceneId":"s1","text":"All the stars she knows by name,"},{"id":"s1-34","sceneId":"s1","text":"End and origin thereof,"},{"id":"s1-35","sceneId":"s1","text":"Knows if love be kin to shame,"},{"id":"s1-36","sceneId":"s1","text":"If shame be less than love."},{"id":"s1-37","sceneId":"s1","text":"What was crooked now is straight,"},{"id":"s1-38","sceneId":"s1","text":"What was rough is plain;"},{"id":"s1-39","sceneId":"s1","text":"Grief and sorrow have no weight"},{"id":"s1-40","sceneId":"s1","text":"Now to cause her pain."},{"id":"s1-41","sceneId":"s1","text":"Plain to her why fevered blisters"},{"id":"s1-42","sceneId":"s1","text":"Made her dark hands run,"},{"id":"s1-43","sceneId":"s1","text":"While her favored, fairer sisters"},{"id":"s1-44","sceneId":"s1","text":"Neither wrought nor spun;"},{"id":"s1-45","sceneId":"s1","text":"Clear to her the hidden reason"},{"id":"s1-46","sceneId":"s1","text":"Men daily fret and toil,"},{"id":"s1-47","sceneId":"s1","text":"5"},{"id":"s1-48","sceneId":"s1","text":"Staving death off for a season"},{"id":"s1-49","sceneId":"s1","text":"Till soil return to soil."},{"id":"s1-50","sceneId":"s1","text":"One to her are flame and frost;"},{"id":"s1-51","sceneId":"s1","text":"Silence is her singing lark;"},{"id":"s1-52","sceneId":"s1","text":"We alone are children, lost,"},{"id":"s1-53","sceneId":"s1","text":"Crying in the dark."},{"id":"s1-54","sceneId":"s1","text":"Varied feature now, and form,"},{"id":"s1-55","sceneId":"s1","text":"Change has bred upon her;"},{"id":"s1-56","sceneId":"s1","text":"Crush no bug nor nauseous worm"},{"id":"s1-57","sceneId":"s1","text":"Lest you tread upon her."},{"id":"s1-58","sceneId":"s1","text":"Pluck no flower lest she scream;"},{"id":"s1-59","sceneId":"s1","text":"Bruise no slender reed,"},{"id":"s1-60","sceneId":"s1","text":"Lest it prove more than it seem,"},{"id":"s1-61","sceneId":"s1","text":"Lest she groan and bleed."},{"id":"s1-62","sceneId":"s1","text":"More than ever trust your brother,"},{"id":"s1-63","sceneId":"s1","text":"Read him golden, pure;"},{"id":"s1-64","sceneId":"s1","text":"It may be she finds no other"},{"id":"s1-65","sceneId":"s1","text":"House so safe and sure."},{"id":"s1-66","sceneId":"s1","text":"Set no poet carving"},{"id":"s1-67","sceneId":"s1","text":"Rhymes to make her laugh;"},{"id":"s1-68","sceneId":"s1","text":"Only live hearts starving"},{"id":"s1-69","sceneId":"s1","text":"Need an epitaph."},{"id":"s1-70","sceneId":"s1","text":"Lay upon her no white stone"},{"id":"s1-71","sceneId":"s1","text":"From a foreign quarry;"},{"id":"s1-72","sceneId":"s1","text":"6"},{"id":"s1-73","sceneId":"s1","text":"Earth and sky be these alone"},{"id":"s1-74","sceneId":"s1","text":"Her obituary."}]}